+## 8. Replay set (bench/build_replay_set.py) — round 11 of 12
+
+Built via `python3 bench/build_replay_set.py` (host, no GPU; read-only on
+recordings + the mem0 SQLite stores in mode=ro). It writes the **gitignored**
+replay bodies to `bench/.replay/m1/agent.jsonl` and `bench/.replay/m1/mem.jsonl`
+(`bench/.replay/` is in `.gitignore`; recorded content stays out of git) and
+the committed manifest to `bench/results/2026-10-12/m1-ngram/replay_manifest.json`.
+
+**Set composition**
+- **agent (30 req, 6 distinct steps, both arms):** `baseline-r0/0` ×5,
+  `baseline-r1/0` ×5, `baseline-r1/2` ×5, `mem0-r0/0` ×5, `mem0-r1/0` ×5,
+  `mem0-r2/0` ×5. Steps chosen by `step_score` (file read/edit/write + test
+  output); turns spread across each step. Each request = one recorded assistant
+  turn: messages = system prompt + full history before the turn, assistant
+  reasoning **kept** as `reasoning_content` (pi-ai converter), `tool_calls` and
+  tool results kept, `tools` = the recorded `toolsAdded`. No sampling params in
+  the body — the probe sets them.
+- **mem (12 req, 5 distinct steps):** 9 `tool_add` (mem0_memory add) + 3
+  `capture` (auto-capture), one per recorded `mem` tap record. System =
+  ADDITIVE_EXTRACTION_PROMPT **verbatim** (recon/mem0_extract_src.txt:11-486,
+  single-pass unescaped). User prompt per mem0_extract_src.txt:838 / :1137-1165
+  (`## Summary` / `## Last k Messages` / `## Recently Extracted Memories []` /
+  `## Existing Memories` / `## New Messages` / `## Observation Date` /
+  `## Current Date` / `# Output:`). Per-call cutoff from the triggering tool
+  (toolAdd ts for `tool_add`; first-text ts for `capture`); existing = latest-10
+  live memories (ADD/UPDATE, DELETE removed) created before the cutoff. Bodies
+  carry `response_format {type:json_object}` +
+  `chat_template_kwargs {enable_thinking:false}`. One capture (`mem0-r0/2/0`)
+  has recorded `predicted_n=2048` (a max_tokens cap hit); the cap is carried
+  only as the recorded `predicted_n`, not as a body sampling param.
+
+**Est/recorded calibration (chars/4 estimator, unchanged)**
+- agent median **0.833** (in 0.75–1.33)
+- mem median **1.027** (in 0.75–1.33)
+- n_messages mismatches vs tap: **0**
+- agent `system_prompt_exact`: **true**
+- agent n_messages<=3 ratios (exact-system turns):
+  0.846, 0.846, 0.84, 0.877, 0.877, 0.877
+
+**Outliers (est/recorded outside 0.75–1.33): 3, all agent**
+| id | est/recorded | recorded_prompt_tokens | effective chars/token |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| inventory-baseline-r0/0/5 | 0.740 | 13032 | 2.96 |
+| inventory-baseline-r0/0/8 | 0.743 | 13939 | 2.97 |
+| inventory-baseline-r0/0/10 | 0.742 | 14317 | 2.97 |
+
+All three are long-code turns of `baseline-r0/step0` (turns 5, 8, 10). Their
+prompts are dominated by long assistant reasoning (~26k chars, mostly code/
+symbolic) plus assistant code text and tool output, so the effective chars per
+token falls to ~2.96–2.97 and the flat chars/4 estimator under-predicts the
+real token count. Code tokenizes at **<4 chars/token** (many 1–2-char symbol
+tokens), so tool-output / code-heavy turns are expected to land below 1 — and
+these three are only marginally below 0.75 (0.740–0.743). No estimator change
+was made; the **median (0.833) passes** with the unchanged chars/4 estimator.
+
+**Reading caveats (advisor, applied this round)**
+- `est_over_recorded_reasoning_after_last_user_only` == `est_over_recorded`
+  for every agent request: each step is a fresh session with a single user
+  message before all assistant turns, so "all reasoning" and "reasoning after
+  the last user message" are the same set. This reflects the recording
+  structure, **not** template evidence.
+- `chars_by_role['reasoning']` is non-zero on the long-output steps (e.g.
+  `baseline-r0/0/5`=25717, `mem0-r2/0/8`=19456), confirming
+  `reasoning_content` is counted and kept in the bodies.
+- `system_prompt_exact` (true) is about the **agent** system prompt, rebuilt
+  from the recorded `sections` map and joined by blank lines
+  (`pi_prompt_src.txt` / `buildSystemPromptSections`); exactness is supported
+  by the n_messages<=3 ratios above. The **mem** system prompt is
+  ADDITIVE_EXTRACTION_PROMPT verbatim.
